{"id":"offenbar","lemma":"offenbar","pos":"adv","rank":1072,"glosses":["apparently, evidently; obviously"],"ipa":"/ˈɔfn̩baːɐ̯/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/2c/De-offenbar.ogg/De-offenbar.ogg.mp3","examples":[{"text":"Du hast offenbar recht.","en":"Apparently you're right.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/760262","words":[{"g":"you"},{"g":"have","l":"haben"},null,{"g":"right, right-hand"}]},{"text":"Das war offenbar eine blöde Idee.","en":"That was obviously a stupid idea.","words":[{"g":"the / that"},{"g":"was","l":"sein"},null,{"g":"a"},{"g":"stupid, dim-witted","l":"blöd"},{"g":"idea"}]},{"text":"Er hat offenbar gelogen.","en":"He obviously lied.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/392547","words":[{"g":"he / it"},{"g":"has","l":"haben"},null,{"g":"untrue"}]},{"text":"Offenbar geht er gerne spazieren.","en":"He must like taking walks.","words":[null,{"g":"to go, to walk","l":"gehen"},{"g":"he / it"},{"g":"don't mention it"},{"g":"to take a walk"}]},{"text":"Es gibt offenbar ein Problem.","en":"There's clearly a problem.","words":[null,null,null,{"g":"a"},{"g":"problem"}],"phrases":[[0,2,"there is, there are"]]}]}